# Tests for the bed centre on an arm that reaches only 5 mm past it
# (arm_crosses_centre, position_min: -5).  The branch changes only at the
# centre, so a tool that has crossed has to come back through the centre
# before it is further out than that.  The planner holds a move that
# takes the tool onto the far side until it sees whether the next ones
# bring it back, and otherwise turns the bed half a turn on the centre -
# which it also does for every line straight across the bed.
#
# test/multi_axis/test_centre_path.py (TestShortReach) checks the plans
# and test_kin_6axis.c runs one through the real step compressor.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG polar_singularity_reach.cfg

G28 X
G28 B
G28 Z
G90
G1 X40 Y0 Z0.3 F6000

# A line across the bed: too long for the far side, so the bed turns
# half a turn on the centre
G1 X-40 Y0 E4 F1500

# Across to 3mm past the centre and straight back: the far side carries
# it both ways and the bed never turns
G1 X40 Y0 F6000
G1 X-3 Y0 E6 F1500
G1 X40 Y0 E10 F1500

# Across to 3mm past, then on along the far side out of reach: planned
# again on the near side, with the half turn on the centre
G1 X-3 Y0 E12 F1500
G1 X-3 Y10 E13 F1500

# The same as travel: back through the centre, off the path, no blob
G1 X40 Y0 F6000
G1 X-3 Y0 F6000
G1 X-3 Y10 F6000

# Onto the far side and then a wait: given up, the half turn made
G1 X40 Y0 F6000
G1 X-3 Y0 E15 F1500
M400
G1 X40 Y0 E19 F1500

GET_POSITION
G1 Z10 F600
M84
